:{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"JCqJFXc2vh"},{"type":"text","value":", which\nuses observational data that are NOT gridded; it plots data at\nobservation points, which are not on a standardized grid. Model output,\non the other hand, is gridded with points at regularly spaced intervals\nin the horizontal as well as the vertical (","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"dpGoKWbV37"},{"type":"crossReference","kind":"figure","identifier":"obsvsgridded","label":"obsvsgridded","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fig. ","key":"hiMxWK0xEL"},{"type":"text","value":"17","key":"bNcTwB9z1A"}],"template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"17","resolved":true,"html_id":"obsvsgridded","key":"ukPvbTLWLi"},{"type":"text","value":").","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"CEaNtmWGNc"}],"key":"CRe4a7t3PU"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"With gridded data (e.g., model output) we can put the computer to work\nto generate contours that will conform to the data instead of having to\ndo all that work by hand analysis from our point observations. This allows\nmeteorologists to make hundreds of analyzed maps quickly that can then\nbe inspected to determine what is happening now and if there are forecast\noutput, then into the future as well!","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"nY6GCcmmeh"}],"key":"N7s1vtGClY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":21,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Our goal in this chapter is to be able to find, access, and understand\nwhat data are contained within gridded files and be able to create\ncontour plots analyzing the data.","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"Lllcc7u277"}],"key":"J6us8yppkw"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/build/obs_versus_gridded_o-393e50f78a8a1add2ccae6b799296669.png","alt":"Gridded versus observations points","width":"750px","align":"center","key":"G8olKDffNB","urlSource":"../../images/obs_versus_gridded_output.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"obsvsgridded","identifier":"obsvsgridded","html_id":"obsvsgridded","enumerator":"17","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"jaxIlOwQT7"},{"type":"text","value":"17","key":"Frppajj58H"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"WtQCt2K51p"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"wnFKbONIZX"},{"type":"text","value":"a) gridded data on regularly spaced grids and b) observations from discrete\nlocations from where those particular observations came from.","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"wEpqNbMMWL"}],"key":"ZbI82RbLh7"}],"key":"tuqDSe6k6L"}],"label":"obsvsgridded","identifier":"obsvsgridded","enumerator":"17","html_id":"obsvsgridded","key":"T5Dt5sxlTy"}],"key":"s1gq725U3m"}],"key":"pNFce65AIy"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Practice Tasks - Forces","url":"/forces-practice-tasks","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"},"next":{"title":"Gridded Data Files","url":"/gridded-data-location","group":"Introduction to Weather Technology using MetPy"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3001"}